  "text": "Airmid was an Irish goddess. She was a healer of the Tuatha Dé Danann, children of the goddess Danu. She was a daughter of the divine physician Dian Cécht. With her brother Miach, she healed the wounded hand of King Nuada. Her father had made a hand of silver. The two children grew real flesh over it. In envy, Dian Cécht killed Miach. Airmid then found healing herbs on her brother's grave. Her father saw her sort the herbs and scattered them. The Irish said the loss of her herb lore made human pain much greater.",
